# mutgap_dec_render_fault_releases_encoder: 200 render execs, each faulting after its encoder exists (0x16 RenderBarrierResources is always unsupported), then a pass that draws: the decoder's fault path ends and releases the encoder, and more faults than a command queue's 64 command buffers leave the next exec to complete. Measured: without the release (a leaked, ended encoder per fault) the draw completes as well, so the leak is not visible to the guest here.
